cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Geryon: measuring prompt-injection defences against within-policy attacks"
message: >-
  If you use this instrument, the attack corpus, or the pair counts it derives,
  please cite it. Cite the upstream work it measures separately: AgentDojo for
  the benchmark, and Progent for the defence.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Luigi
    family-names: Iacuaniello
    email: luigi@a3thinker.it
repository-code: "https://github.com/luiacuaniello/geryon"
abstract: >-
  An instrument for measuring action-level prompt-injection defences on the
  subset of attacks that reach the attacker's goal using only actions the agent
  was already authorised to take. Such attacks are 9% of AgentDojo; a
  tool-identity policy cannot see them, and no published evaluation reports a
  separate number on them. Includes a pre-registered protocol, a within-policy
  attack corpus, a seeded adaptive attacker, and pilot measurements of Progent
  and of one deployed MCP gateway.
keywords:
  - prompt-injection
  - llm-security
  - ai-agents
  - security-evaluation
  - model-context-protocol
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-03"
